(9. RAG Pipeline Explained) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 697 Tm
(RAG means Retrieval Augmented Generation.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 679 Tm
(In this project, RAG works like this:) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 661 Tm
(1. The incoming ticket text is converted into an embedding.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 648 Tm
(2. The embedding is compared against the ChromaDB vector collection.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 635 Tm
(3. The retriever fetches the top matching knowledge base chunks.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 622 Tm
(4. A distance score is converted into a similarity score.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 609 Tm
(5. If the best score is at least 0.50, RAG is considered strong enough.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 596 Tm
(6. The retrieved chunks are formatted as context.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 583 Tm
(7. The LLM is prompted to use only the internal knowledge base context.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 570 Tm
(8. The LLM response is converted into up to six suggested solution steps.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 552 Tm
(Important files:) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 534 Tm
(- backend/rag/retreiver.py) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 521 Tm
(- backend/rag/augmentation.py) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 508 Tm
(- backend/rag/vector_store.py) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 495 Tm
(- backend/rag/embeddings.py) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 482 Tm
(- backend/llm/groq.py) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 464 Tm
(Why this matters:) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 446 Tm
(- It keeps answers grounded in internal support knowledge.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 433 Tm
(- It provides source tracking through rag_sources.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 10 Tf
1 0 0 1 54 420 Tm
(- It gives admins a rag_score to understand match quality.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 8 Tf
1 0 0 1 518 28 Tm
(Page 11) Tj
ET
